# OpenSSL (Ruby's openssl): built in, so nothing here; this file is kept so that `require "openssl"` works as in Ruby.
#
#   Ruby                                          Sake
#   OpenSSL::HMAC.hexdigest("SHA256", key, data)  the same (also digest, base64digest)
#   OpenSSL::KDF.pbkdf2_hmac(pw, salt:, iterations:, length:, hash: "sha256")   the same
#   OpenSSL::PKCS5.pbkdf2_hmac(pw, salt, iter, len, "sha1")                     the same
#   c = OpenSSL::Cipher.new("aes-256-gcm"); c.encrypt; c.key = k               OpenSSL::Cipher.encrypt(c); OpenSSL::Cipher.set_key(c, k)
#
# A digest is named by a String (MD5, SHA1, SHA256, SHA384, SHA512, any case), not an OpenSSL::Digest object; an
# unknown name raises OpenSSL::Digest::DigestError. See docs/manual/en/ref/OpenSSL-HMAC.md and OpenSSL-Cipher.md.
# Until 2026-10-20 HMAC was written here in Sake over sakelib/digest.sake (about 20 ms per HMAC).
